{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Look to.</b> Rabbi Jonah said that תחוללכם is a future form like תשובבכם, in place of the past חוללתכם, and Rabbi Moses the Kohen said that it is an adjective, and if there is no parallel of its pattern:" "<b>and I will bless him.</b> The vav is punctuated with pataḥ because it is future, and the meaning is 'I said to him and I will bless him,' and so it was <small>(and so)</small>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {0 "The comment ends abruptly with an unresolved conditional; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:56.090074456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}